# CODEOWNERS — who reviews what.
#
# This file names the reviewers a pull request must be approved by before it can
# be merged. It only has force once the branch protection rule on `main` is set
# to "Require review from Code Owners" (see docs/git-workflow.md, §7).
#
# Replace the placeholder owners below with the department's own GitHub accounts
# when the repository is handed over. Until then they resolve to the maintainer,
# and nobody can approve their own pull request — so at least two people with
# write access are needed for the gate to mean anything.

# Default owner for everything in the repository: the maintainer.
*                       @yonz2

# The laboratory procedures. Every change to a document of record is reviewed by
# a laboratory code owner — the head of the laboratory, or a PLP they nominate.
/sop/                   @yonz2

# The renderer and the form template. A change here changes every document the
# pipeline produces, so it is reviewed with the same care as a document.
/document-pipeline/     @yonz2
